{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>As Aaron your brother was gathered.</b> על אשר לא קדשתם — thus it is written in Rashi's commentary. But this verse is not here; rather, it is in the portion of Ha'azinu, and here it is written כאשר מריתם פי וגו׳. But according to the halakhah in the Sifrei it works out fine: כאשר מריתם פי במדבר צין — Rabbi Shimon ben Elazar says: Moses and Aaron too died by הכרת, as it says על אשר לא קדשתם אותי — the inference: if you had sanctified Me, your time to depart had not yet arrived. And perhaps out of respect for Moses and Aaron, Rashi did not cite the statement of Rabbi Shimon ben Elazar, but only the conclusion of the matter."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "חז״‎ק appears to be an abbreviation for a phrase meaning 'but it is known/established'; rendered here as 'But' introducing the objection. The reference to Rashi appears to point to Rashi's comments on this verse, where על אשר לא קדשתם is cited."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:00.000416426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}